  "campaign": {
    "title": "THE QUIET LEDGER",
    "story": "The Quiet Ledger was never a bank. It was a private intelligence brokerage that sold protection to the highest bidder, and for eleven years its officers moved dossiers, bought silence, and buried a single manifest: a ledger of every bribe, every black operation, every name that had been paid to look away. That manifest surfaced at Meridian Transit Hub in the hands of a courier with a one-way ticket out of the city. You were hired to lift it before it left the platform.\n\nThen the Ledger's auditor, Mara Vance, began reconciling the books at Halcyon Archive. She found the name of the man who had hired you at the top of the payor list. The contract changed overnight: silence the auditor before she could copy the backup. You took the job. But inside the vault you read her notes and learned the truth — she was not embezzling. She was building a case against the entire network, and Director Halden, your own handler, was its architect. You lowered the blade. You staged her death, and the Ledger believed her dead.\n\nNow Halden knows a witness still breathes. Mara — the \"asset\" — is hidden in a coastal glasshouse while a cleanup team closes the net. Your new contract is to extract her before they do. The twist is that the asset is the woman you were paid to kill, and the manifest's true author is the handler who hired you. Deliver her to Halden and the Ledger survives; deliver her anywhere else and it burns. This time the destination is yours to choose."
  },
